From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: web pages see Linux in the user agent

Web pages are told NickelOS's browser runs on Linux, not ChromeOS: the
user agent's platform is "X11; Linux x86_64" (the reduced user agent) or
"Linux <cpu>" (the full one), and its client hints say platform "Linux",
with no platform version, as Chrome on Linux does.

Linux apps run natively on NickelOS, and sites that see ChromeOS send a
Chromebook's choices. Dresden found it with Slack (2026-11-09): signing
in from Slack's Linux app opens the browser, and Slack's sign-in page sent
a ChromeOS browser to Slack's web client within a second, instead of
back to the app (slack://), which works (ChromeOS's protocol prompt, then
nickel-appd starts the app). "Open in app" links and download pages
(Zoom, Teams, Discord) do the same.

ChromeOS's own pages (Settings, setup, Files, the Terminal) are unaffected:
WebUI decides it runs on ChromeOS when it is built
(ui/webui/resources/js/platform.ts, <if expr="is_chromeos">); its isLinux,
read from the user agent, is used by no ChromeOS page. navigator.platform
already said "Linux x86_64".

diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
index bf4a896..b7fda1c 100644
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
@@ -276,7 +276,7 @@ std::string GetUserAgentPlatform() {
 }
 
 std::string GetUnifiedPlatform() {
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   // This constant is only used on Android (desktop) and Linux.
   constexpr char kUnifiedPlatformChromeOSX64[] = "X11; CrOS x86_64 14541.0.0";
 
@@ -293,7 +293,8 @@ std::string GetUnifiedPlatform() {
   }
   return "Linux; Android 10; K";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-  return kUnifiedPlatformChromeOSX64;
+  // NickelOS: web pages see Linux (see GetPlatformForUAMetadata()).
+  return "X11; Linux x86_64";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
   return "Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_7";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
@@ -590,7 +591,8 @@ std::string GetPlatformVersion() {
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
   return GetWindowsPlatformVersion();
-#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+  // NickelOS: no ChromeOS version for web pages, as on Linux.
   return std::string();
 #else
 
@@ -619,14 +621,13 @@ std::string GetPlatformForUAMetadata() {
   // "macOS" by default
   return "macOS";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-  // TODO(crbug.com/40846294): The branding change to remove the space caused a
-  // regression that's solved here. Ideally, we would just use the new OS name
-  // without the space here too, but that needs a launch plan.
-#if BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING)
-  return "Chrome OS";
-#else
-  return "Chromium OS";
-#endif
+  // NickelOS: web pages are told Linux. Linux apps run natively here, and
+  // sites that see ChromeOS send a Chromebook's choices: Slack's sign-in
+  // from its Linux app went to Slack's web client instead of back to the
+  // app, and "open in app" links and download pages offer Android apps or
+  // nothing. ChromeOS's own pages decide they're on ChromeOS when they are
+  // built (ui/webui/resources/js/platform.ts), not from the user agent.
+  return "Linux";
 #else
   return std::string(version_info::GetOSType());
 #endif
@@ -790,10 +791,9 @@ std::string BuildOSCpuInfoFromOSVersionAndCpuType(const std::string& os_version,
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
                       "%s Mac OS X %s", cpu_type.c_str(), os_version.c_str()
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-                      "CrOS "
-                      "%s %s",
-                      cpu_type.c_str(),  // e.g. i686
-                      os_version.c_str()
+                      // NickelOS: Linux, as on Linux.
+                      "Linux %s",
+                      cpu_type.c_str()  // e.g. i686
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
                       "Android %s", os_version.c_str()
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
